From 47f09e8f61d2583eef9a92dae6015d95917159ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:50:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 68/97] XNotify: filtered XNotifyGetNext no longer leaves the
 listener signalled for notifications it did not ask for

WWE '13's XMP listener only dequeues 0x0A000003. A custom song start broadcasts 0x0A000001/2 to it; the
manual-reset wait handle was only reset when the whole queue emptied, so the title's notification worker
busy-spun (sub_83240C38: 2 calls before the play request, 43.7 million after) and starved the game's audio -
all game audio silent after a custom entrance song. The filtered dequeue now resets the handle when the
requested id is absent or exhausted; non-matching notifications stay queued for an unfiltered GetNext.

Also opt-in, rate-limited diagnostics (default off): REX_XMP_STATE_PROBE=1 (XMP answers/notifications),
REX_AUDIO_FRAME_PROBE=1 (per-second guest/output audio levels).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
